  "rationale": "Proposed blocking set: jumpHost:lateralMovement, secretsManager:privilegeEscalation, printServer:lateralMovement, appServer:lateralMovement, fileServer:lateralMovement. The target is an OR of four collection steps, so each must be cut. (1) vaultRead needs jumpHost or secretsManager; blocking both cuts it, and blocking jumpHost also stops domainAdmin. (2) shareMount depends only on secretsManager, so it is cut. (3) dbReplica needs hypervisor, printServer or serviceAccount. Blocking printServer removes one route. Blocking appServer stops hypervisor and serviceAccount, because both require appServer as an AND parent. (4) mailArchive needs domainAdmin, printServer or fileServer, and all three are now cut. That makes 5 blocks. I did not prove 4 is impossible. I checked the obvious shared chokepoints and none of them saves a block. Blocking dmzWeb kills apiToken, rdpLogin and secretsManager, but fileServer stays reachable through dbLogin, so it still totals 5. Blocking ciRunner covers apiToken and dbLogin but not rdpLogin, also still 5. No single step cuts both the hypervisor/serviceAccount route and the fileServer route. printServer is reachable through configSecret, ssoLogin and apiToken, so it cannot be cut further upstream."
